# Station (live server): room 1's dismantling terminal at -52.9,34.4, from the user's recording of 2026-11-15
# (.work/e2e/202650-record, 121-138 s, where the user dismantled a Vesta 4P): the terminal opens the dismantle window
# (the client's MANUFACTURE_ITEM_CATAGORY) beside the cargo; an item dragged onto 'Place Item Here' (INVENTORY_MOVE on
# the button-up; the server's ITEM_BASEs: the window shows the parts it would give back, the cost, Dismantle) and
# '<<Inv' takes it back (MANUFACTURE_ACTION) without dismantling it, so the cargo does not change. The close box;
# home. Needs an item that dismantles (ammunition and ore do not: nothing is sent): a Vesta 4P in cargo column 2,
# row 2, put there once with the GM command `/createitem 3246 1` (2026-11-18).
name: starbase dismantling: an item placed and taken back
timeout: 300
include _sb_home
walk-to -50,25
walk-to -52.9,34.4
face 102
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 20
click 548,533 until antprox 'received MANUFACTURE_ITEM_CATAGORY' every 2 within 20
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 20
shot dismantle_open
# the Vesta 4P (cargo column 2, row 2) dragged onto 'Place Item Here'
down 136,520
wait-quiet proxy 0.3 within 5
up 370,640
expect-event antprox 'received INVENTORY_MOVE' within 10
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 20
shot dismantle_placed
click 380,435
expect-event antprox 'received MANUFACTURE_ACTION' within 10
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 20
shot dismantle_back
click 866,277
expect-event antprox 'received MANUFACTURE_ACTION' within 10
wait-quiet proxy 1.0 within 20
walk-to -50,25
walk-to -48,5
